cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sunborn in your research, production systems, or academic benchmarks, please cite it as below."
title: "Sunborn: Deterministic Equivalence, Multi-Tier Semantic Caching, and Partial Execution Reuse for Agentic RAG Systems"
abstract: >-
  Sunborn is a high-performance distributed semantic execution gateway designed around formal equivalence
  classes (C0 to C3). It integrates RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS), Non-Exchangeable Conformal Risk
  Control with 32-byte ContextDigest context-lineage binding, SIMD-accelerated 64-bit Roaring Bitmaps for microsecond
  transitive key closure, cost-aware Greedy-Dual-Size-Frequency (GDSF) eviction, and Non-Accelerator Authority
  over PostgreSQL state. Sunborn guarantees zero cross-tenant leakage, 0.0% semantic false hits under calibrated
  guardrails, and sub-millisecond execution reuse across frontier LLMs (Claude, Gemini, OpenAI).
